<!-- Intro -->
<div class="mb-12">
<p class="text-gray-300 text-lg leading-relaxed font-light">
                                    Ephemera is built on the core principle that <strong class="text-white font-medium">privacy is a fundamental human right</strong>. Unlike traditional email providers that mine your data for advertising, Ephemera is designed to know as little about you as possible. This policy outlines exactly what we do—and more importantly, what we don't do—with your data.
                                </p>
</div>
<!-- Section 1 -->
<div class="scroll-mt-28 mb-16 border-b border-white/5 pb-12 last:border-0" id="collection">
<div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-3xl">dataset</span>
<h2 class="text-white text-3xl font-display font-bold">1. Data Collection</h2>
</div>
<div class="space-y-4 text-gray-300 leading-7">
<p>
                                        We practice strict data minimization. We only collect the absolute minimum information necessary to provide our service.
                                    </p>
<ul class="list-none space-y-3 mt-4">
<li class="flex items-start gap-3">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-sm mt-1">check_circle</span>
<span><strong>Account Information:</strong> If you create a premium account, we store a hashed version of your password and your chosen username.</span>
</li>
<li class="flex items-start gap-3">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-sm mt-1">check_circle</span>
<span><strong>Payment Data:</strong> Payment processing is handled by third-party providers (Stripe/Crypto). We do not store full credit card numbers on our servers.</span>
</li>
<li class="flex items-start gap-3">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-sm mt-1">check_circle</span>
<span><strong>Temporary Logs:</strong> Server logs are flushed every 24 hours and contain no personally identifiable information (PII).</span>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<!-- Section 2 -->
<div class="scroll-mt-28 mb-16 border-b border-white/5 pb-12 last:border-0" id="usage">
<div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-3xl">settings_applications</span>
<h2 class="text-white text-3xl font-display font-bold">2. Use of Information</h2>
</div>
<div class="space-y-4 text-gray-300 leading-7">
<p>
                                        The information we collect is used solely for the purpose of operating the Ephemera service. We do not use your data for profiling, advertising, or marketing.
                                    </p>
<p>
                                        Your disposable email addresses and the content within them are processed automatically to deliver messages to you. Once a disposable session expires or is manually deleted, all associated data is permanently erased from our active memory and databases.
                                    </p>
</div>
</div>
<!-- Section 3 -->
<div class="scroll-mt-28 mb-16 border-b border-white/5 pb-12 last:border-0" id="zero-knowledge">
<div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-3xl">lock</span>
<h2 class="text-white text-3xl font-display font-bold">3. Zero-Knowledge Architecture</h2>
</div>
<div class="bg-primary/5 border border-primary/20 rounded-xl p-6 mb-6">
<p class="text-primary-100 font-medium">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined align-middle mr-1">info</span>
                                        Note: We cannot recover lost passwords because we never knew them in the first place.
                                    </p>
</div>
<div class="space-y-4 text-gray-300 leading-7">
<p>
                                        Ephemera employs a zero-knowledge architecture for all stored emails. This means that all emails are encrypted on the client side before they ever reach our servers.
                                    </p>
<p>
                                        We utilize <strong>AES-256 encryption</strong> for data at rest and <strong>TLS 1.3</strong> for data in transit. The decryption keys are derived from your master password, which is never sent to our servers. Consequently, Ephemera staff, government agencies, or hackers cannot read your emails even if they gain access to our physical servers.
                                    </p>
</div>
</div>
<!-- Section 4 -->
<div class="scroll-mt-28 mb-16 border-b border-white/5 pb-12 last:border-0" id="third-party">
<div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-3xl">share</span>
<h2 class="text-white text-3xl font-display font-bold">4. Third-Party Disclosures</h2>
</div>
<div class="space-y-4 text-gray-300 leading-7">
<p>
                                        We do not sell, trade, or otherwise transfer your personally identifiable information to outside parties. This does not include trusted third parties who assist us in operating our website, conducting our business, or servicing you, so long as those parties agree to keep this information confidential.
                                    </p>
<p>
                                        We may release your information when we believe release is appropriate to comply with the law, enforce our site policies, or protect ours or others' rights, property, or safety. However, due to our zero-knowledge architecture, the "information" we can release is extremely limited.
                                    </p>
</div>
</div>
<!-- Section 5 -->
